                            Preamble

  The GNU Affero General Public License is a free, copyleft license for
software and other kinds of works, designed specifically to ensure
cooperation with the community in the case of network server software.

  The licenses for most software and other practical works are designed
to take away your freedom to share and change the works.  By contrast,
our General Public Licenses are intended to guarantee your freedom to
share and change all versions of a program--to make sure it remains free
software for all its users.

  When we speak of free software, we are referring to freedom, not
price.  Our General Public Licenses are designed to make sure that you
have the freedom to distribute copies of free software (and charge for
them if you wish), that you receive source code or can get it if you
want it, that you can change the software or use pieces of it in new
free programs, and that you are thinking of the same things.

  Developers that use our General Public Licenses protect your rights
with two steps: (1) assert copyright on the software, and (2) offer you
this License which gives you legal permission to copy, distribute and/or
modify the software.

  A secondary benefit of traditional free software licenses is that
developers who make improvements to the software are encouraged to
share them with the community.  In the case of network server software,
this is less effective.  If you modify network server software and let
users interact with it remotely over a network, you might not be
distributing the modified software.  Therefore, we have developed the
GNU Affero General Public License.  The GNU Affero General Public License
is the same as the GNU General Public License with the additional
requirement that if you run a modified program on a server and let other
users interact with it remotely through a network, your server must
provide them with the opportunity to receive the Source Code of your
version.

  The precise terms and conditions for copying, distribution and
modification follow.

